9606830dba635ffab95479"} {"question" "q-1070" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the coefficient matrix for the following system of linear equations?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2}+4{x}_{1}=3{x}_{3} \\\\ -11{x}_{3}=12\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035972/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec6b1bb1ec5a1ac5954b9a5ded7ad10b4860eb090b9606830dba635ffab95479"} {"question" "q-1070" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we organize the system so that the variables are ordered ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}-11{x}_{3}=12\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -11\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035972/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec6b1bb1ec5a1ac5954b9a5ded7ad10b4860eb090b9606830dba635ffab95479"} {"question" "q-1070" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035972/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "58a528cff20e81240a29618a2501db1a7e744090acb230fd24881e525813dbbf"} {"question" "q-1070" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035972/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec6b1bb1ec5a1ac5954b9a5ded7ad10b4860eb090b9606830dba635ffab95479"} {"question" "q-1070" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -11 & 12\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -11\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -11 & 12\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -11\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -11\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035972/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec6b1bb1ec5a1ac5954b9a5ded7ad10b4860eb090b9606830dba635ffab95479"} {"question" "q-1070" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -11\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035972/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec6b1bb1ec5a1ac5954b9a5ded7ad10b4860eb090b9606830dba635ffab95479"} {"question" "e-4683" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the coefficient matrix for the following system of linear equations?\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2y=1 \\\\ 2y=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035972/example-4683.json" "file_sha256" "dc5d4e321cae8e575c9ca658a84b759cc401a99055496f0ef592117bc4e0c08d"} {"question" "e-4683" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we organize the system so that every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-2y=1 \\\\ 0x+2y=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n\\left\\lbrack\n\t\\matrix {\n\t\t1 & -2 \\\n\t\t0 & 2 \n\t}\n\t\\right\\rbrack\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035972/example-4683.json" "file_sha256" "dc5d4e321cae8e575c9ca658a84b759cc401a99055496f0ef592117bc4e0c08d"} {"question" "e-4684" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the augmented matrix for the following system of linear equations?\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y+x-5-3z=0 \\\\ z=y+7x \\\\ y+3-2z=1-2x\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035972/example-4684.json" "file_sha256" "9b988ce643282dd0153f1f344a76b8a500898c767740f2d2c97a9946a9c95c61"} {"question" "e-4684" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we organize the system so that the variables are ordered $x,y,z$ on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y-3z=5 \\\\ -7x-y+z=0 \\\\ 2x+y-2z=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n\\left\\lbrack\n\t\\matrix {\n\t\t1 & 1 & -3 \\\n\t\t-7 & -1 & 1 \\\n                2 & 1 & -2 \n\t}\n\t\\right\\rbrack\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix  is the coefficient matrix augmented with the column that represents the right-hand sides of the equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -7 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035972/example-4684.json" "file_sha256" "9b988ce643282dd0153f1f344a76b8a500898c767740f2d2c97a9946a9c95c61"} {"question" "e-4685" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What would be the system of equations for the following augmented matrix?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & -4 & -12 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035972/example-4685.json" "file_sha256" "3e6886b91c7d5615edb91ab306e15ac3c0115fad3463286235dd677951605bcb"} {"question" "e-4685" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The augmented matrix consists of two parts: the coefficient matrix and the column of constants.\n\nThe coefficient matrix represents the coefficients in the linear system, while the column of constants represents the constants on the right-hand sides of the equations.\n\nUsing the variables $x$ and $y,$ then, the corresponding system of equations is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-4y=-12 \\\\ 3x+y=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035972/example-4685.json" "file_sha256" "3e6886b91c7d5615edb91ab306e15ac3c0115fad3463286235dd677951605bcb"} {"question" "e-4686" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the augmented matrix for the following system of linear equations?\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{c}{2}=a \\\\ 5+3b-a=4c \\\\ d=1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035972/example-4686.json" "file_sha256" "c2c15cc45f3647acb0d1957db9f0cf4f6c1b7f573e81409ae43b63adaf027045"} {"question" "e-4686" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we organize the system so that the variables are ordered $a,b,c,d$ on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-a+0b+\\frac{1}{2}c+0d=0 \\\\ -a+3b-4c+0d=-5 \\\\ 0a+0b+0c+d=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix is the coefficient matrix augmented with the column that represents the right-hand sides of the equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -4 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 