of the equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -7 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [17592186059502 :question/problem "What would be the system of equations for the following augmented matrix?\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -4 & -12 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186059502 :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix consists of two parts: the coefficient matrix and the column of constants.\n\nThe coefficient matrix represents the coefficients in the linear system, while the column of constants represents the constants on the right-hand sides of the equations.\n\nUsing the variables $x$ and $y$, then, the corresponding system of equations is\n\n$$\n5x - 4y =-12; 3x + y = 1\n$$"] [17592186059503 :question/problem "What is the augmented matrix for the following system of linear equations?\n\n${\\frac{c}{2} = a; 5 + 3b - a = 4c; d = 1$"] [17592186059503 :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that the variables are ordered $a,b,c,d$ on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n-a + 0b + \\frac{1}{2}c + 0d = 0; - a + 3b - 4c + 0d =-5; 0a + 0b + 0c + d = 1\n$$\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix is the coefficient matrix augmented with the column that represents the right-hand sides of the equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -4 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186056085 17592186056086 17592186056087 17592186056088 17592186056089 17592186057554 17592186057555 17592186057556 17592186057557 17592186057558 17592186058916 17592186058917 17592186058918 17592186058919 17592186058920] "immutable_fields" [[17592186056084 :answer-field/correct] [17592186056084 :answer-field/id] [17592186056084 :answer-field/ke